1.Transaction Processing System (TPS)
 -Customer Sales Transactions
 -Payment Processing
 -Goods Receiving
 -Stock Dispatches 

2.Management Information Systems (MIS) & Decision Support Systems (DSS): 
 -MIS Tracking: Store management utilizes a Management Information System (MIS) to view structured weekly sales reports aggregated by department.

 -DSS Assistance: A Decision Support System (DSS) uses analytical models to run "what-if" simulations. It helps management evaluate how a promotion will affect profit margins,
  inventory levels, and competitor reactions before launch.

3.Executive Support Systems (ESS):
 -Static Reports: Annual financial performance summaries and overall market share overviews.

 -Competitor Data: Competitor pricing adjustments, regional expansion tracking, and market positioning data.

 -Long-Term Forecasts: 5-year consumer trend projections and macroeconomic retail growth forecasts.

4.KWS & Office Automation (OAS)
 -Knowledge Work System (KWS): Computer-Aided Design (CAD) software used by retail space designers to optimize store layouts and shelf placements.

 -Office Automation System (OAS): Microsoft 365 / Google Workspace used by administrative staff for daily email communication, document typing, and shift scheduling.

